branch: a-transient-map-view-has-an-owner

kq's cost_golden_decode moves view_frees from 0 to 4, and what it buys is that
those four sorted views are no longer leaked. The counter counts frees, so it
rises when memory is reclaimed — nothing kq allocates changes, and every other
counter in both of its goldens is byte-identical.

The gain is much larger where maps are transient than it is here: kanso's own
oneshot benchmark moves the same counter 0 to 2,761. kq's decode mostly builds
its maps outside any beat, where there is no rewind to free at, so it keeps the
document-bounded views it always had.
